  m_Name: SpaceExploration
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  exhibitName: Space Exploration
  description: "Space Exploration is the investigation of outer space using advanced
    technology such as rockets, satellites, and telescopes.The first artificial satellite,
    Sputnik 1, was launched by the Soviet Union in 1957. In 1961, Yuri Gagarin became
    the first human in space. Today, exploration includes the International Space
    Station, robotic missions to Mars, and telescopes like Hubble and James Webb.
    \r\nSpacecraft are designed to survive harsh conditions such as vacuum, radiation,
    and extreme temperatures. Missions aim to expand knowledge of the universe, search
    for extraterrestrial life, and develop technology for future interplanetary travel."
  audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: b7c7be331081d10498e66ffa30e1a06e, type: 3}
